  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_031 (multimodal, scvi_n200 + VIT_L, concat) at 0.532 acc, but it only marginally exceeds RNA-only scvi_n200 (config_024, 0.520 acc), suggesting the image contribution is small and the fusion strategy may be a bottleneck. All multimodal results used concat fusion; weighted fusion is untested. Question: config_017 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while keeping the exact same encoders (scvi_n200 + VIT_L) and singleprofile setting as config_031, giving a clean A/B comparison that isolates the effect of fusion strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly extends the top-performing configuration with a single-variable change, maximizing information per experiment. (2) If weighted fusion improves meaningfully over concat, it reveals a lever for further optimization and justifies exploring weighted fusion in multiprofile settings. (3) If it does not improve, it indicates the current encoder pair is near its ceiling with simple fusion, redirecting effort toward multiprofile aggregation or alternative RNA encoders. (4) Under a limited budget, this minimal-change comparison is more informative than jumping to a multiprofile or new-encoder configuration that would confound multiple variables."
}

